  "scope": "Fence all five AnalyzeScript cast writers and their nested mutations by the active Storyboard root and actual organization/parent relationships.",
  "upstreamExisting": [
    "Organization characters/looks/voices and attached/shared cast",
    "Organization locations, matching/linking and orphan cleanup",
    "Generated element placeholders, histories/pointers/claims, activity and unchanged replay policies"
  ],
  "implemented": [
    "Narrow storyboardCast(owner) surface binds five writers and rejects supplied sequence ids outside the immutable owner.",
    "SQL-time organization/sequence/root-or-explicit-trusted-claim/processing guards reach identity/history/link INSERTs, pointers, statuses, claim demotion and activity.",
    "Actual character/cast, look/character/cast and location/link relationships constrain existing targets. Internal initial ids and matched/orphan location paths use the appropriate root-plus-organization admission.",
    "Character/look default backfill, legacy features move, independent incoming voice-description batch, look revival/retirement, location repoint/conflict deletion and separate orphan cleanup are included.",
    "Generated element conditional INSERT retains schema defaults and encoding. Multi-look INSERTs remain in one atomic D1 batch while staying under per-statement parameter limits.",
    "AnalyzeScript passes its existing resolved root to createCastRecords. A withOwnership bracket checks empty/reused/error results; every actual write remains separately guarded.",
    "Shared retry/cause/abort protocol is retained, with confirmed loss converted to NonRetryableError inside create-cast-records. Ownerless behavior, service operation order, sharing and claim/history policies remain."
  ],
